From cdd609dc5eff4fc6b44fec0f07f265e95dbae5cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moto <j3tm0t0@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 06:46:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] netpipe: bridge mode (proxy ARP for the Z's IP, forward
 IPv4 between SLIP and Wi-Fi)

The Z sends its IP in the request header. Frames for that IP are taken
from the Wi-Fi netif before lwIP, SLIP-encoded and queued for the Z; ARP
requests for it are answered with the Pico's MAC; the Z's packets go out
with etharp_output. Inbound ICMP echo requests are dropped (ESP/X hangs
on them after closing a TCP connection). UDP mode stays as the fallback
when the field is 0. TX pbufs now come from PBUF_POOL instead of the
4000-byte MEM heap.
---
 src/netpipe.c | 305 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 267 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/netpipe.c b/src/netpipe.c
index ad14c57..93ef1d9 100644
--- a/src/netpipe.c
+++ b/src/netpipe.c
@@ -1,11 +1,18 @@
 /*
- * netpipe.c -- SCSI ID 6 の空き LBA 帯を使って、X68000 Z と Wi-Fi 側のホストの間でバイト列 (SLIP) を運ぶ
+ * netpipe.c -- SCSI ID 6 の空き LBA 帯を使って、X68000 Z (slipd.x -z) と Wi-Fi の間で SLIP を運ぶ
  *
- * X68000 Z (slipd.x -z) は 1 回の交換で
+ * X68000 Z は 1 回の交換で
